INSERT INTO `entity_contents` VALUES ('06af1bbf-51fe-4c60-ba65-41319f6d','academic','ffabb298-25af-4a2e-8af2-c27848df','Master\'s Convocation Ceremony: Pokhara University','Attended the Master\'s Convocation Ceremony at Pokhara University, celebrating the successful completion of postgraduate studies and the achievement of an important academic milestone. The event recognised academic excellence and marked the formal conferment of the master\'s degree.',2),('0ff60b22-50a6-408a-85ef-2329c6dd','project','44513486-14da-4092-b385-13ba0ec0','','',0),('1c27bf1b-6c66-4f1e-ad04-178cc9b7','academic','94195fc6-5e29-4258-b89b-2a69fec0','Density-Based Traffic Light System Demonstration (Competition)','Demonstrated a density-based traffic light control system at a technical competition, showcasing the use of ultrasonic sensors to detect vehicle density and dynamically adjust traffic signal timings. Presented the working prototype, explained its real-world applications in reducing traffic congestion through sensor-based automation, and effectively communicated the system\'s design, functionality, and implementation to judges and attendees. The demonstration highlighted practical problem-solving, teamwork, and technical presentation skills.',2),('1f3e6c01-bd72-4fb3-ba43-a6bccecc','project','3e1035d4-4914-41b0-bed1-3919c190','','',0),('26661c15-ae6e-4dc9-98e2-fad2405e','academic','be44239f-eb2a-41a9-b014-559a16a7','Prom Night Participant','Participated in the organisation and celebration of the school\'s annual prom night, demonstrating teamwork, communication, and social engagement.',0),('4007e430-4a9d-4e7d-8021-fc53920d','academic','ffabb298-25af-4a2e-8af2-c27848df','Fuzzy Logic-Based Horizontal Fragmentation in Distributed Databases','Published a research paper in the International Journal of Advanced Social Sciences on improving horizontal fragmentation in distributed database systems using fuzzy logic and precedence values. The study proposed an efficient data fragmentation approach to optimise data distribution, balance network load, and enhance the performance of distributed database systems.',0),('5e81d359-02cb-4ef9-9563-aed51aef','project','bf5782f5-8f35-4904-905a-a3cb6277','','',0),('6bac19e5-54b7-4e3a-b38f-a161bc9b','achievement','da837d90-712b-40b6-b582-0f956a36','Best Minor Project – Density-Based Traffic Light Control System','Developed and demonstrated a Density-Based Traffic Light Control System that uses ultrasonic sensors to detect vehicle density and dynamically adjust traffic signal timings. The project aimed to reduce traffic congestion, minimize unnecessary waiting time, and improve road safety through sensor-based automation. Successfully presented the working prototype, system architecture, and real-world applications during a technical competition, showcasing problem-solving, teamwork, and technical presentation skills.',0),('6fb1a32b-a7bf-41d4-a532-c9bed045','academic','94195fc6-5e29-4258-b89b-2a69fec0','Minor Project on Density-Based Traffic Control System:','Developed a density-based traffic control system using ultrasonic sensors to detect vehicle density and automatically switch traffic signals based on real-time traffic conditions. The project focused on improving traffic flow and reducing congestion through sensor-based automation. Successfully designed, implemented, and tested the prototype as part of a team, and the project was recognised with the Best Minor Project award for its innovation and practical application.\n',1),('74dc67c8-5384-4a41-bc79-b868c249','achievement','2327e20d-9367-4140-9928-5c7188d4','Organizer, Reviewer & Manager – KEC Conference 2025 (2082)','Served as a Multirole Contributor for KEC Conference 2025 (2082), taking responsibilities as an Organizer, Paper Reviewer, and Manager. Contributed to conference planning, coordination, and execution while reviewing research papers for technical quality, relevance, and academic standards. Managed various academic and operational activities, coordinated with teams and participants, and supported the successful organization of the conference while maintaining research and publication quality.',1),('83ed190e-dd3c-450f-883f-9c7193a5','project','7e0a7a45-5cda-49e7-b04c-b4ecf6c3','','',0),('9bc99e69-535c-4191-84fe-e14681f4','project','89297556-b96d-4003-8581-4c174162','','',0),('a8847bbc-62f5-4542-b1ee-f70df40b','project','efae7d74-bb3f-43a6-9c26-9ae9755b','','',0),('aec89fe0-e5ea-4258-8468-31e5118b','achievement','ef6845ea-33f3-4baa-a084-93fd7c84','Organizer Member – KEC LITE Technical Exhibition','Served as an Organizer Member for KEC LITE Technical Exhibition at Kantipur Engineering College, contributing to the successful planning and execution of the event. Coordinated with organizing teams, managed technical activities, supported project demonstrations, assisted participants with exhibition requirements, and helped ensure smooth event operations. Played an active role in creating a platform for students to showcase innovative engineering projects while developing skills in teamwork, event management, coordination, and technical communication.\n',1),('b0faec86-55e4-4ec3-9b8d-fad89f45','academic','94195fc6-5e29-4258-b89b-2a69fec0','Yagi-Uda Antenna Design and Fabrication for TV Signal Reception','Designed, fabricated, and tested a Yagi-Uda directional antenna for terrestrial TV signal reception, specifically tuned to receive Kantipur TV broadcasts. Calculated antenna element dimensions and spacing based on the operating frequency, assembled the antenna, and evaluated its performance through practical testing. Optimised the design to improve signal strength, directivity, and reception quality while applying principles of antenna theory and wireless communication.',0),('b128b7f6-2469-4581-b3e7-576fa8b8','achievement','2327e20d-9367-4140-9928-5c7188d4','Organizer & IT Head – KEC Conference 2021 and 2022','Served as the IT Head and Organizing Committee Member for KEC Conference 2021 and 2022 at Kantipur Engineering College. Managed the technical infrastructure of the conference, handled IT-related operations, coordinated digital platforms, and supported smooth communication and event execution. Collaborated with the organizing team to plan and conduct conference activities, ensuring efficient management of technical requirements and successful delivery of the academic event.',0),('c0b93d9d-bcd7-44f5-82f3-400b46a3','achievement','ef6845ea-33f3-4baa-a084-93fd7c84','Judge – KEC LITE 2021 & 2022 Technical Exhibition','Served as a Judge for KEC LITE 2021 and KEC LITE 2022 at Kantipur Engineering College, evaluating innovative student projects across various engineering domains. Reviewed project concepts, technical implementations, practical applications, and presentation quality. Provided constructive feedback to participants, assessed project performance based on technical creativity and problem-solving approaches, and contributed to maintaining the quality and standards of the technical exhibition. This role enhanced my experience in project evaluation, technical analysis, and mentoring aspiring engineers.',0),('c1592519-7a79-4c21-9c80-865119c1','academic','ccf47170-aea4-452f-a437-d9f50833','Cultural Field Trip :Patan Durbar Square Case Study','Participated in a cultural field trip and conducted a case study on the history of Patan Durbar Square, enhancing research, observation, and cultural heritage knowledge.',3),('c6c84b3d-badd-476f-8aa5-b78bb05b','project','b7dbe8ee-6aac-48da-b054-58d15a3c','','',0),('cc8db7e6-de4f-488a-a3c8-3a2af5ce','academic','94195fc6-5e29-4258-b89b-2a69fec0','Graduation Ceremony (TU 44th Convocation)','Attended the graduation ceremony upon the successful completion of the Bachelor of Engineering programme, marking the achievement of academic and professional milestones.',4),('cd121a61-f4d4-4d37-a4c4-7391ca74','project','7e63dbdb-2120-4af9-95cd-e5aa3faa','','',0),('ce045991-b9f1-4d6d-aeaf-984fc461','academic','ccf47170-aea4-452f-a437-d9f50833','Talent Show','participated in a talent show as a guitarist, performing in front of an audience. This experience strengthened my confidence, stage presence, and ability to perform under pressure. It also demonstrated my dedication, creativity, and teamwork while showcasing my passion for music and continuous self-imvement.',1),('d1cdb343-20b3-4a44-95c9-d379e95b','achievement','da837d90-712b-40b6-b582-0f956a36',' Best Major Project – EMG-Based Bio-Robotic Arm for Prosthetic Applications','\nDesigned and developed an EMG-Based Bio-Robotic Arm that captures electromyography (EMG) signals from human muscles to control a robotic arm in real time. The system integrates EMG sensors, a microcontroller, and servo motors to replicate natural arm movements, offering a low-cost prosthetic solution for amputees. The adaptable control architecture can also be extended to lower-limb prosthetic applications with minimal modifications, demonstrating innovation in biomedical engineering, embedded systems, and assistive robotics.\n',1),('d31ecdd6-ce1f-49b1-ab83-b688cb7d','academic','ccf47170-aea4-452f-a437-d9f50833','Cultural Talent Show: Boys vs. Girls Mandala Making Competition','Participated in a team-based mandala making competition, demonstrating creativity, teamwork, and artistic skills.',2),('da0e6277-400c-4cbc-b5b3-66e18c89','academic','ccf47170-aea4-452f-a437-d9f50833','Class 1','Class 1 Group Photo',0),('de31d720-6eeb-4684-b85d-a0cc2213','achievement','cbe19331-ce6d-4635-bd16-ca67a78a','Featured as the Face of the College','Featured as the **Face of the College** and appeared in official college promotional materials, including the **college calendar, banners, and social media posts**, representing student achievements, academic excellence, and institutional pride.\n',0),('f87a4a0b-61c3-44c7-88b6-ad669739','academic','ffabb298-25af-4a2e-8af2-c27848df','Overall Excellence Award for Academic Achievement','Received the Overall Excellence Result Award in recognition of outstanding academic performance and consistent achievement throughout the academic programme. The award acknowledges dedication, hard work, and excellence in maintaining a high standard of academic success.',1),('f8bd4590-6314-433e-b28d-fefa1912','academic','94195fc6-5e29-4258-b89b-2a69fec0','EMG-Based Bio-Robotic Arm for Prosthetic Applications','Designed and developed an EMG-based bio-robotic arm that replicates the natural movements of a human arm by capturing and processing electromyography (EMG) signals from muscles. Integrated EMG sensors, a microcontroller, and servo motors to translate muscle activity into real-time robotic arm movements, providing a low-cost prosthetic solution for amputees. The control system was designed to be adaptable, allowing the same hardware and signal-processing approach to be tuned for lower-limb prosthetic applications with minimal modifications.',3);
