INSERT INTO `entity_promotion_contents` VALUES ('03cda8bf-fb57-4662-8c8f-82a0c236','3f5317cb-ca34-4ee6-a3c1-0e014520','Quality Control Officer at NBTC(National Building and trade Center)','Responsible for **CAD design, network design, and technical consulting** for communication, internet, CCTV, and fire alarm system projects. Prepared detailed design drawings, reviewed system layouts, provided technical solutions, and supported project implementation according to specifications and industry standards. Conducted design reviews, coordinated with engineering teams, and provided consultancy support to ensure reliable, efficient, and high-quality system installations.\n',0),('0a041702-bc9b-43f6-98b9-abf27793','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','Co author on Paper \"ExerLiteNet: Lightweight CNN-LSTM Architecture for Binary Exercise Recognition from Webcam RGB Video,\"','The paper presents a lightweight deep learning approach that combines MobileNetV3Small and LSTM networks to recognize exercises such as squats and bicep curls from standard RGB webcam video. The work demonstrates how efficient AI models can achieve strong performance while remaining practical for deployment on everyday hardware.\n\nPublishing research is a significant milestone that reflects dedication, persistence, and a commitment to advancing knowledge. Wishing the authors continued success in their future research endeavors and professional growth.\nDOI: https://lnkd.in/gUbpsXhA',13),('0f5adf7b-dce2-4fce-bba0-f6e21109','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','Project supervision for Major Project (Facial Recognition Based Attendance System)','Facial Recognition-Based Attendance System (2024) based on MTCNN\n\nObjective:\n\nThe main goal of the Facial Recognition-Based Attendance System using MTCNN (Multi-task Cascaded Convolutional Networks) is to provide an automated, secure, and efficient way to manage attendance. The system will utilize face recognition technology to identify individuals, ensuring that attendance is recorded in real-time.\n\n\n\nSpecific Objectives:\n\n\n\nTo develop a system that automatically recognizes the faces of individuals, eliminating the need for manual roll calls or identification methods.\n\nTo update the attendance of individuals in real-time, offering an efficient solution for tracking presence.\n\nFeatures:\n\nThe Facial Recognition-Based Attendance System boasts several advanced features designed to optimize the attendance process:\n\n\n\nFace Recognition:\n\nUsing MTCNN, the system identifies individuals based on their facial features, offering accurate and reliable recognition, even in varying lighting conditions.\n\nReal-Time Attendance Recording:\n\nAs soon as the system recognizes an individual’s face, their attendance is automatically recorded in real time, ensuring that attendance logs are updated instantly.\n\nAutomated Attendance Tracking:\n\nThe system eliminates manual entry, reducing human error and ensuring that records are consistently accurate, secure, and tamper-proof.\n\nStudents Involved:\n\n\n\nAnupam Roka Magar\n\nCimrika Bajracharya\n\nKusum Ghimire\n\nNeha Rauniyar\n\n',1),('27c33c80-941b-4f05-9f29-28a7b6d7','d76b7a6b-bf6d-4421-82be-d06948f3','Low voltage system design at Techno craft PVT Ltd','specialising in the design and development of low-voltage electrical and ELV systems. Responsibilities included preparing CAD drawings, network and telecommunication designs, fire alarm system layouts, smart energy meter network designs, and electrical load calculations. Also involved in the design of DG systems, electrical panels, and single-line diagrams, while coordinating with engineering teams to ensure accurate, efficient, and standards-compliant design solutions.',0),('2e36c7c0-6fcf-4c5a-964b-08d982ce','b7478010-225b-4f64-99f4-8f1108da','Author of paper Kec Conference 2023','**Author – KEC Conference 2023**\nCo-authored the research paper titled **“Comparison of Machine Learning Algorithms for Classification of Data Traffics in Software Defined Networks”**, presented and published at the **KEC Conference 2023: International Conference on Engineering and Technology**. The research focused on evaluating machine learning algorithms for efficient classification and analysis of network traffic in Software Defined Networks (SDN).',1),('38294f45-367b-4497-ae9d-e31401cd','07af2004-beb1-49da-800c-992cbdd9','Served as an Assistant Lecturer ','Promoted from **Lab Assistant to Assistant Lecturer** in recognition of strong performance and dedication. Served as an **Assistant Lecturer** for **Filter Design**, delivering lectures and conducting laboratory sessions for **Computer Network and Security, Distributed Systems,** and **Filter Design**. Provided academic guidance and supported students in practical learning and technical development.\n',0),('3d24d684-8f3a-4a7b-802d-c8f78006','648249c1-9e2e-49e9-a084-9e65362a','Ward Darta and Chalani (Ward3, Ward 5, Ward 15, Ward 23)','Developed and maintained **full-stack applications** using **React, Electron, Node.js, and Express**, delivering dynamic web and cross-platform desktop solutions. Designed responsive user interfaces with **Tailwind CSS** and implemented backend services with **RESTful APIs** for seamless frontend and backend communication. Managed **PostgreSQL databases** using **Sequelize ORM**, including data modelling, migrations, and query handling. Implemented secure authentication and authorization strategies, optimized application performance, and managed deployments on **DigitalOcean EC2** with **Samba-based file sharing** for local development workflows. Integrated **Jenkins CI/CD pipelines** and **Grafana monitoring** to automate deployments, track system performance, and improve application reliability.\n',3),('5cd81a26-c535-48a0-9d68-fc53acf6','648249c1-9e2e-49e9-a084-9e65362a','PaigeApp (An Israel based Full Stack Development Application)','Developed and maintained a full-stack mobile and web application using React, React Native, Node.js, and Express to deliver dynamic user experiences across platforms. Designed responsive interfaces using Tailwind CSS and developed scalable backend services with RESTful APIs. Managed PostgreSQL databases using Sequelize ORM, including database modelling, migrations, and query handling. Implemented secure authentication and authorization mechanisms, optimized application performance through code splitting and lazy loading, and monitored and resolved application issues to improve reliability and user experience. Contributed to cross-platform application development and deployment for both web and mobile platforms.\n\nWeb Link: http://Paigeapp.com Play Store: https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.paigemob&hl=en IOS Store: https://apps.apple.com/us/app/paige-the-last-food-fight/id6469138670',1),('5fea148a-04f4-4e98-8711-42baf992','01da1b0c-ed4e-41de-bca5-2d66e72c','Aircraft Maintenance Engineering Internship','Completed an internship at **Shree Airlines**, supporting **Aircraft Maintenance Administration (AMA)** and **Aircraft Maintenance Control (AMC)** activities. Assisted in maintaining aircraft technical records, updating the technical library with approved maintenance manuals and documentation, organising maintenance records, and ensuring accurate documentation in compliance with aviation regulations. Gained practical exposure to aircraft maintenance documentation, record management, and maintenance planning processes while supporting engineering and maintenance teams.\n',0),('6805f234-4cd4-4153-b37a-7c715ec7','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','Paper Reviewer for Kec Journal 2025','Served as a **Paper Reviewer for the KEC Journal 2025 (Volume 3)**, responsible for evaluating research manuscripts, reviewing technical content, assessing originality, quality, and relevance of submissions, and providing constructive feedback to support the publication of high-quality research articles.',10),('6ee5e5f4-e675-4242-a0e2-91c355c9','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','Organizer – KEC LITE 2081','Served as an Organizer for KEC LITE 2081 at Kantipur Engineering College, contributing to the successful planning and execution of the event. Coordinated with teams, supported project demonstrations, managed technical activities, and assisted students in showcasing innovative engineering projects during the event.',3),('803955dd-bd1c-46ad-a3f7-80af4e36','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','Conducted Training on Web Development & Hosting for KEC Faculty','Together with my colleague Er. Aliz Shrestha, we conducted a focused training session for the faculty members of Kantipur Engineering College (KEC), aimed at enhancing their digital competencies in web development and hosting.\n\nTraining Highlights:\nPortfolio Website Development:\nHelped participants create their own professional portfolio websites using user-friendly tools and platforms suitable for non-developers.\n\nBlog Platform Setup:\nIntroduced the setup and management of personal or academic blogs, covering content creation, organization, and platform selection.\n\nLearning Management System (LMS) Integration:\nProvided guidance on setting up and using LMS platforms for online course delivery, assignment management, and student interaction.\n\nWeb Hosting & Deployment:\nCovered practical aspects of shared hosting, including domain name registration (especially .np domains), DNS configuration, and site deployment using control panel-based tools like cPanel.\n\nThis training was designed to equip faculty with hands-on knowledge to independently manage their online platforms for academic and professional use.',7),('86f664bd-db66-4087-8681-b653a3cc','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','Journal Paper on Entanglement to Disentanglement: Evaluating the Performance of Traditional VAE vs. Modified Beta-VAE','Traditional VAEs, while powerful, often struggle to separate features within the latent space, leading to entangled representations that reduce interpretability and hinder performance, particularly in tasks like image compression.\nIn this study, we explore advanced VAE models, specifically the β-VAE, which aim to improve disentanglement for clearer and more interpretable latent representations. However, the results also highlight an inherent trade-off: while disentanglement improves, it can lead to a decline in reconstruction quality. The research emphasizes the importance of hyperparameter optimization to balance the benefits of clearer feature separation with the quality of reconstructed outputs.\nKey contributions of the paper:\nEvaluating how β-VAE reduces latent space entanglement.\nAnalyzing the delicate balance between disentanglement and reconstruction quality.\nProviding insights into the optimization strategies required to get the best of both worlds.\nThis work opens the door for future research into improving the balance between interpretability and performance, which is crucial for applications in image compression, data representation, and AI model interpretability.\n🔗https://lnkd.in/dU2Vn-5a\nDOI: https://lnkd.in/d4kmtTvi',6),('95037a80-e095-4f21-a28b-2c10ef39','145b15d6-f143-4afe-977f-c6d76adc','VSAT Engineer','Worked as a **VSAT Support Engineer** under the **VSAT and Radio Department**, responsible for VSAT network channel management and satellite communication support for clients including **NMB Bank, Smart Cell, NB Bank, Annapurna Base Camp, and Nepal Rastra Bank (NRB)** across remote districts such as **Manang, Solukhumbu, Okhaldhunga, and Ramechhap**. Performed VSAT installation, configuration, monitoring, and maintenance, including **iDirect VSAT system configuration, carrier monitoring, bandwidth management, and link optimisation**. Designed and supported network setups using **Cisco, Raisecom, and MikroTik** devices, including routing, switching, and connectivity troubleshooting. Provided L2 technical support for hub and remote sites, ensuring reliable satellite communication, network performance, and operational availability.\n',0),('98915339-7364-4586-966f-3859fe93','648249c1-9e2e-49e9-a084-9e65362a','Clinic CMLT (Us based Project as a Senior Backend Developer)','Developed and maintained **backend services** using **Node.js and Express**, building scalable web applications with **Next.js** for server-side rendering and static site generation. Designed and managed **PostgreSQL databases**, including schema design, data optimisation, and query performance improvements. Created responsive user interfaces using **Tailwind CSS**, developed **RESTful APIs** for frontend integration, and implemented secure **authentication and authorization** mechanisms to ensure reliable application access.',0),('a0779952-3155-4dd7-8d6d-810bd50b','648249c1-9e2e-49e9-a084-9e65362a','Ward3 Lab report Management System (Application made for lalitpur Ward 3)','Developed and maintained full-stack applications using **React, Electron, Node.js, and Express**, creating responsive user interfaces and cross-platform desktop solutions. Designed and integrated **RESTful APIs**, managed databases using **Sequelize ORM with PostgreSQL**, including data modelling and migrations. Implemented secure authentication and authorization mechanisms, optimized application performance through efficient coding practices, and monitored, troubleshot, and improved application reliability and user experience.\n\nweb: https://whic.lmcityward3.com/lab',2),('a3771a87-29c7-4022-9747-0c206f39','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','First Letters of Recommendation for EMAI & M.Sc. Programs','Wrote Letters of Recommendation (LoRs) for outstanding students applying to prestigious international master\'s programs. This includes a successful recommendation for the Erasmus Mundus Joint Master Degree in Artificial Intelligence (EMAI), and another for a master\'s program in Communication Engineering and Data Science (application submitted via Aalto CODAS / FullFabric platform). These endorsements supported strong candidates pursuing advanced studies in cutting-edge fields across Europe.',8),('aeee4122-db75-4afc-85f4-e2dbac66','b7478010-225b-4f64-99f4-8f1108da','Organinzing Comitte for Kec Conference 2021 and 2022','Serves as IT Head',0),('af3a3508-8ab8-4d3c-b8b2-e047f71a','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','Project Supervisor: “VISIOLEX: Crafting Context-Aware Captions from Images”','Served as the Project Supervisor for the final-year project titled “VISIOLEX: Crafting Context-Aware Captions from Images” at Kantipur Engineering College. Provided technical guidance, project supervision, and academic support to the project team consisting of Nitesh Kamat, Rushal Parajuli, Soumya Dahal, and Suraj Bhattarai. Guided students throughout the project lifecycle, including research, system design, implementation, documentation, and presentation, ensuring technical quality, practical relevance, and adherence to academic standards.',11),('b37a20bf-a20b-4166-8d33-a48a434c','68a7475e-53ff-433e-9299-f6d8bc3c','Constultant work for Pokhara Goodwill Apartment, KTC','Provided **smart energy meter design and technical consultancy** for **Pokhara Goodwill Apartment**, including meter network planning, system architecture design, communication layout, and integration requirements. Prepared design solutions, reviewed technical specifications, and coordinated with project teams to ensure efficient energy monitoring, accurate data communication, and reliable smart metering system implementation.\n',0),('b3f8bb15-745b-4472-8f0c-553d0e39','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','Project supervision for Major Project (Dynamic Traffic Mangmenent Based on YoloV8)','Dynamic Traffic Management based on YOLOv8 (2024)\n\nObjectives:\n\nThe aim of the Dynamic Traffic Management System based on YOLOv8 (You Only Look Once version 8) is to optimize traffic flow and ensure smoother, safer roads, especially in high-density areas.\n\n\n\nMain Objectives:\n\n\n\nTo create an adaptive traffic management system that can intelligently prioritize lanes with higher traffic volume.\n\nTo ensure emergency vehicles can navigate traffic efficiently by providing them with special priority, improving emergency response times.\n\nApplications:\n\nThe proposed dynamic traffic management system has several important applications:\n\n\n\nPriority for High-Density Lanes:\n\nThe system prioritizes lanes with a higher number of vehicles, improving scheduling and reducing congestion on busy roads.\n\nSpecial Controls for Emergency Vehicles:\n\nEmergency vehicles, such as ambulances or fire trucks, are given immediate priority, ensuring that they are not delayed by traffic and can reach their destination swiftly.\n\nStudents Involved:\n\n\n\nAbikal Aryal\n\nAnuj Koirala\n\nPradip Dahal',0),('b723897a-068c-4959-9d73-0c1fac79','648249c1-9e2e-49e9-a084-9e65362a','NerdStudyhub','Developed and managed Nerd Study Hub, an online education platform designed to provide study notes, learning materials, and academic resources for Computer Engineering, Electronics Engineering, BCA, and CSIT students. The platform focuses on delivering structured course content, interactive notes, discussion features, and video-based learning resources to enhance students\' academic experience. Designed to support knowledge sharing, student engagement, and easy access to quality educational materials through a digital learning environment.\nweb: https://nerdstudyhub.com/',4),('bd5eb8cd-0bd9-4bae-9fbe-076f51d0','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','Journal Paper on Forearm Bio-Medical Signal Processing','This work explores an innovative approach to analyzing forearm muscle signals using both EMG and EEG data, collected via ECG electrodes. By combining these signals, we gain new insights into motor control and muscle activity, ultimately enhancing the precision of robotic prosthetic systems.\nKey highlights:\nEEG helps track brain activity, focusing on alpha and beta waves, essential for motor planning and execution.\nEMG analyzes muscle activity and is key to monitoring muscle contractions in real-time.\nCombining both improves event-related potentials (ERPs) for more accurate forearm movement control, paving the way for assistive technologies that can enhance neurorehabilitation and upper limb mobility.\nThis research offers potential applications in fields like industrial equipment management, medical rehabilitation, and assistive technologies for those with limb disabilities.\nI\'m excited to explore how these findings can transform biofeedback systems and improve the quality of life for individuals with motor impairments.\n🔗 https://lnkd.in/dnC__k-8\nDOI: https://lnkd.in/dV59qBj3',5),('c1ad1d22-13a7-4bfc-9ed4-3e2859c4','1a2e940f-2680-4f70-8470-e8da23ad','Lab Assistant ','Served as a **Lab Assistant** for **Computer Networks, Communication II, Data Communication, Filter Design,** and **C++ Programming**, providing lab support, preparing exercises, and assisting students with practical learning.\n',0),('cb44b42e-95b9-459e-bf4b-ba2aa92b','b7478010-225b-4f64-99f4-8f1108da','CoAuthor of paper Kec Conference 2023','**Co-Author – KEC Conference 2023**\nCo-authored the research paper titled **“Prediction of DDoS Attacks in IPv6 Based SDN Network using Hybrid Machine Learning Technology”**, presented and published at the **KEC Conference 2023: International Conference on Engineering and Technology**. The research focused on applying hybrid machine learning techniques for predicting and detecting DDoS attacks in IPv6-based Software Defined Networks (SDN).\n',2),('cc3cf650-3f3f-40df-8b7d-62518419','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','Kec Conference 2025 (2082) Organizer and Reviewer','**Multirole Contributor – Organizer, Reviewer & Manager, KEC Conference 2025**\nServed as a **Multirole Contributor** for **KEC Conference 2025**, taking responsibilities as an **Organizer, Paper Reviewer, and Manager**. Contributed to conference planning, coordination, and execution; reviewed research papers for technical quality and relevance; and managed various academic and operational activities to ensure the successful organisation of the conference.\n',4),('cf6858d2-a295-45f1-852b-b31b5c04','b7478010-225b-4f64-99f4-8f1108da','Paper Reviewer for Kec Conference 2024','Served as a **Paper Reviewer for the KEC Conference 2024**, responsible for evaluating research papers, reviewing technical content, assessing originality and quality, and providing constructive feedback to support the selection of high-quality research contributions for the conference.\n',4),('cfe2f21d-de6b-4c02-ba0f-99a48b73','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','Co-author of Paper YOLOv8 vs. Sensor-Based Traffic Control: Kalman Filter Integration for Hybrid Management','The work looks at how traffic lights can be made smarter by using two different approaches: sensors for pedestrians and computer vision for vehicles. By combining these methods, they show how traffic flow can be improved, delays can be reduced, and roads can be made more efficient in busy city areas.\n\nThis achievement reflects their hard work, curiosity, and commitment to learning. It’s great to see their efforts turn into a published paper, and I’m excited to watch them grow further in their research journey.',9),('d5472042-0a6f-497f-800a-8da5f107','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','Featured in College Advertisement','Selected to appear in the college\'s official promotional advertisement in recognition of outstanding academic performance, technical achievements, and active participation in engineering projects. Represented the institution by showcasing student innovation, project excellence, and contributions to academic and extracurricular activities.\n',14),('de0a82ec-7894-4444-9582-f71bd1a5','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','Paper Reviewer for Kec Conference 2026','Served as a **Paper Reviewer for the 8th KEC Conference 2026**, responsible for evaluating research papers, reviewing technical content, assessing originality, quality, and relevance of submissions, and providing constructive feedback to support the selection and publication of high-quality research contributions for the conference.\n',12),('e03d7af3-920d-4541-9887-8626349a','a5de3dce-3164-4cbf-8284-06403e1f','Best Supervisor 2081(Electronics)','**Best Project Supervisor – “Dynamic Traffic Management”**\nRecognised as the **Best Supervisor** for the project **“Dynamic Traffic Management”** by providing technical guidance, project mentoring, and continuous support throughout the development process. Guided students in project planning, implementation, problem-solving, and presentation while ensuring the project achieved its technical objectives and practical relevance.',2),('e8c78105-43f5-4695-9515-30c5ad9a','896fa81b-bd49-426e-a759-6f4aba40','React Developer and DevOps','Started my career as a **System Engineer**, managing servers, infrastructure, and IT operations. As the organization transitioned from traditional server environments to **cloud-based infrastructure**, I evolved into a **DevOps role**, focusing on cloud deployment, automation, and container management. While working with containerized environments, I expanded my skills into **frontend development using React.js**, gaining experience in building modern web applications and integrating development practices with DevOps workflows.',0),('ec70f641-9c1e-4e2f-8750-5faa1e4f','b7478010-225b-4f64-99f4-8f1108da','Paper Reviewer for Kec Conference 2023','Served as a **Paper Reviewer for the KEC Conference 2023**, responsible for evaluating research papers, reviewing technical content, assessing originality and quality, and providing constructive feedback to support the selection of high-quality research contributions for the conference.\n',3);
